=== p2-windows · W7 · page:analytics/YearReview (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:analytics/YearReview   kind=page   web route=/year-review/:year
Web source  : web/src/features/analytics/pages/YearReviewPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300), maui-windows workload installed — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  ApiLogsPage / FeedbackQueuePage / SchemaDriftPage / VehicleCostPage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "YearReviewPage.xaml + YearReviewPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Analytics" is mapped onto these real
  conventions. A fifth file YearReviewPage.SlideFactory.cs hosts the ISlideContentFactory (a UI-construction
  concern, kept beside the view). The surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name
  ("YearReview", already in RouteTable.cs L85 -> /year-review/:year) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs; the registration
  reads the :year route param from ShellViewModel.Current.Param("year") (web Number(yearParam) || current year)
  and wires CloseRequested -> GoBack() (web navigate(-1)).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the two manifest data sources are useVehicles (GET /vehicles) + useYearReview
  (GET /analytics/year-review [year, vehicle_id]). The view-model composes them through an injected
  IYearReviewPageFeed: it loads the vehicle list, auto-selects the first vehicle when none is chosen (web
  useEffect), then reads the year-review for the selected vehicle (web useYearReview enabled: !!vehicleId). The
  default EmptyYearReviewPageFeed resolves the empty/loading state, and the generated-client-backed
  YearReviewPageClientFeed (YearReviewPage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI contract client operations
  Operations.Vehicles.List (get_api_v1_vehicles) + Operations.Analytics.YearReview
  (get_api_v1_analytics_year_review), passing the snake_case year + vehicle_id query params exactly as the web
  hook does (asserted via the FakeFeed). Routes confirmed in internal/api/router.go (/vehicles,
  /analytics/year-review). No HTTP touches the view; a non-success response surfaces as ApiException and the
  view-model renders the native InfoBar+Retry error branch.
- The response is wrapped by the platform httputil.Respond envelope as {data:{…}}; YearReviewReport.FromJson
  unwraps the {data:…} envelope before reading total_drives / total_charge_sessions / year, and keeps the full
  unwrapped object in Raw so the hosted slide deck reads every other field from the SAME single fetch (the native
  analogue of the web threading one resolved `data` object into every slide).
- The web page is a full-bleed story player (the EXCEPTION comment in the web source: a full-screen route that
  intentionally covers app chrome). The native port reproduces every region as visible Fluent regions on a black
  Mica-free overlay (web bg-black) per ADR-006: loading -> centred TsSpinner with the localized "Building your
  year in review…" caption; no-data (web total_drives===0 && total_charge_sessions===0) -> the 🚗 glyph + the
  localized noData line + noDataHint + a Go Back TsButton; error (native robustness branch, never blank) ->
  TsQueryError InfoBar + Retry -> RefreshAsync; success -> the swipe deck: the segmented progress bar, the vehicle
  TsSelect (shown only for >1 vehicle, web vehicleList.length>1), the SlideRenderer deck host, the 1/3 tap zones
  (web w-1/3 cursor zones), the prev/next chevron buttons (web ChevronLeft/Right, shown at the deck ends), the
  close button (web X), the slide counter (web "{i+1} / {n}") and the AI narration mount.
- The SlideRenderer (its own W-prompt, already in-repo) is a pure dispatcher fed by an ISlideContentFactory. The
  parent story player owns the ordered 12-entry SLIDE_DEFS deck (YearReviewSlideDeck.Slides, a verbatim port of
  web review/slides.ts) and wires YearReviewSlideContentFactory, which builds each sibling slide from the single
  resolved YearReviewReport.Raw: the presentational slides (TitleSlide, StatChartSlide, DriveHighlightSlide,
  ChargingBreakdownSlide, EnvironmentSlide, SummarySlide) receive a model parsed from the shared JSON, and the
  cache-then-network slides (StatHeroSlide, SavingsSlide, PatternsSlide) receive a fixed in-memory source that
  replays the same payload as one Loaded emission (so no slide re-fetches). The 'comparisons' kind has no native
  sibling surface yet (its own future prompt), so the factory returns null and SlideRenderer falls back to its
  never-blank localized empty surface — never a blank box.
- SI units (P1/S5): no unit-bearing physical value is formatted by the page shell itself (the slides own their
  conversions); the active UnitPref is resolved once from AppSettingsHost.Current.ToUnitPref() and threaded to the
  unit-aware slides (DriveHighlightSlide/StatHeroSlide/SummarySlide/PatternsSlide) at the display boundary.
- Live data (ADR-013): neither data source is live (useYearReview is STALE-cached static analytics, useVehicles
  is not streamed), so no SSE subscription / >2-min staleness indicator applies to this page.
- i18n (ADR-014): all nine manifest keys already exist verbatim in Strings/en/Resources.resw as
  translation.yearReview.{close,goBack,loading,next,noData,noDataHint,pageTitle,prev,selectVehicle} (added by the
  earlier year-review slide prompts); the page resolves each through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names
  and the same English defaults, so zero literals are hardcoded and no catalog change was needed. The ar/he
  catalogs fall back to the English default via ILocalizer until translated.
- a11y (ADR-015): AutomationProperties names on the page (state-aware), the close/prev/next buttons + tap zones
  (+ tooltips), the vehicle selector and the error surface; keyboard ←/→/Space/Esc nav (web window keydown) and
  pointer tap zones; the surface is a focusable Group automation peer; the black overlay uses an explicit
  white-opacity ramp (never a theme token that would invert under the light theme), the same approach the sibling
  SlideRenderer documents for its always-dark canvas.
- Microsoft.UI-free Model/Source/ViewModel links were added to TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (the WinUI view +
  slide factory are excluded — they use Microsoft.UI); the page's own JsonReads helper (internal, this surface)
  does the null-tolerant parsing.
- Build-time defects found + fixed in this surface's own new code (no red shipped): (1) DispatcherQueue was
  ambiguous between Microsoft.UI.Dispatching and Windows.System (the latter imported for VirtualKey) — fully
  qualified to Microsoft.UI.Dispatching.DispatcherQueue; (2) the app project enforces CA1822/CA1859 as errors, so
  ResolveUnits was made static, the unused VM Slides accessor was inlined, and the three fixed-source builders were
  given concrete return types; (3) an unused _localizer field (CS0414) and unused usings were removed; (4) the new
  files were authored CRLF and normalized to LF via dotnet format. All repaired; the solution builds 0 errors.

=== PARITY ===
PARITY_REQUIRED=12

# Data states (3) — loading / empty / success, each a visible region (never blank); + the native error branch
[x] state  - loading   -> YearReviewPageState.Loading + YearReviewPageDisplay.ShowLoading (projection:
             HasError? no, !HasReport -> Loading); rendered YearReviewPage.cs#_loadingHost (TsSpinner, Label =
             LoadingText "Building your year in review…"); tests State_loading_when_no_report_yet +
             ViewModel_no_vehicles_stays_loading
[x] state  - empty     -> YearReviewPageState.Empty + ShowEmpty (projection: HasReport && Report.HasNoActivity,
             web total_drives===0 && total_charge_sessions===0); rendered _emptyHost (🚗 _emptyEmoji + _emptyTitle
             NoDataText + _emptyHint NoDataHintText + _goBackButton); tests State_empty_when_review_has_no_activity +
             ViewModel_no_activity_review_is_the_empty_state
[x] state  - success   -> YearReviewPageState.Success + ShowSuccess (projection: HasReport && activity); rendered
             _successHost (the swipe deck: _progressGrid + _vehicleSelect + _slideRenderer (SlideRenderer fed by
             YearReviewSlideContentFactory) + tap zones + _prevButton/_nextButton + _closeButton + _counter +
             _aiNarration); tests State_success_when_review_has_activity +
             ViewModel_loads_vehicles_auto_selects_first_and_reaches_success
#   (+ native robustness branch, not one of the 3 required: YearReviewPageState.Error + ShowError ->
#    _errorHost TsQueryError + Retry -> RefreshAsync; tests State_error_takes_precedence_over_loading +
#    ViewModel_feed_failure_is_the_error_state)

